Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:42:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] Sync the liveness engine: a cancel during a device
 restart no longer leaves the camera on (R5, task 30)

Engine from Mosip26 review-fixes-1029 (engine commit 5777716, "Part 3: a cancel during a device restart no longer
leaves the source started"). In a session, a Retry after a device error restarts the camera. A cancel that landed
between the restart's stop and its start left CameraXFrameSource started after the session ended, with its
display listener holding the Activity. The session now stops the source again if it was released meanwhile.

- The four engine jars were built in the review-fixes worktree with git-commit-id skipped (the plugin cannot read a
  git worktree). So they carry no git.properties; nothing reads it at runtime.
- engine-sync.txt has the engine commit and the jars' SHA-256. The models and the camera source are unchanged.
- :liveness:testDebugUnitTest: 123 passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
